{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1539662-hungry-undead-strength","id":1539662,"title":"Hungry Undead Strength","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-01T14:14:05-07:00","id":1539662,"title":"Hungry Undead Strength","content":"How long do the banes gained from activating Undead Strength last for? Can you activate the same Undead Strength bonus multiple times? So could you get a +7 to physical actions at the cost of taking 7 banes? I'm assuming you can't take the same banes more than once at any given time? I'm assuming the vampires in Curseborn can walk around in broad daylight all they want as long as they don't take the 'sunlight' bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T01:59:14-07:00","id":1539740,"title":"","content":"The ashcan got a bit of errata that cleared some of this up. To answer all though that. Both effects last for a scene. You can activate it multiple times and do need to take a different bane for each activation. The real cost here is that it's also 7 Curse Dice which exceeds you cap to start with. Yeah, probably vampires can walk in the sun fine. Some families might alter that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27505-dragox27","name":"Dragox27","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27505_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T03:26:22-07:00","id":1539742,"title":"","content":"Undead strength lasts until the end of the scene, while bane lasts until the end of the game, so maybe that's how they balance it out.<br /> Choosing bane may be a Storyguide.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say that you can choose which calamities you've acquired.<br /> It doesn't say that you can remove the calamities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","user":"veiros","date":". 08-03-2024, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25958-veiros","name":"veiros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25958_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T18:04:25-07:00","id":1539773,"title":"","content":"So, if the banes only last a scene, you just pick the ones that won't affect you, which means they'll never be an issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T16:23:58-07:00","id":1539894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1539662-hungry-undead-strength?p=1539773#post1539773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if the banes only last a scene, you just pick the ones that won't affect you, which means they'll never be an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you pick the ones that won't affect you, the ST is highly encouraged to retcon the scene or reveal elements that screw you over, shortly before using their height advantage over the munchkin to bop you on the head with a rubber mallet. <br /> <br /> Seriously, that's outlined directly. &quot;You are now vulnerable to crossing running open water in New Vegas, but with a lurch, you realize you are standing over a sewer.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:18:38-07:00","id":1539902,"title":"","content":"Also note that there's a cap of +5 Enhancement to any single dice roll. And that includes from Inheritances, edges, spells, or equipment. So, if you use have a gun that gives you a +3 Enhancement, and then activate Undead Strength seven times.... only two of those uses will work alongside that gun.<br /> <br /> Not usually relevant, but its also worth mentioning that Enhancements (including the ones from Undead Strength) only apply after the roll. So you need at least one success on the roll before you can apply any Enhancements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}